I walk on and see a small stall.
A man is selling ceramics here.
The plates and cups are very beautiful.
Everything here is handmade.
I take a blue cup in my hand.
The colour is great.
I look at the seller and ask.
"Excuse me, how much does this cup cost?"
The seller smiles warmly.
"The cup costs thirty-five euros," he says.
Thirty-five euros?
That is unfortunately very expensive.
I do not have that much money for a cup.
I carefully put the cup back.
"That is unfortunately too expensive for me," I say.
"No problem," the seller answers.
"Have a nice day!"
"Perhaps next week," I say and walk on.
